                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p Tot(C)_\bullet
              is a non-negatively graded chain complex with filtration bounded below. Therefore the spectral sequence converges as claimed by the general discussion at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+complex#ConvergenceGeneral"} spectral sequence of a filtered complex - convergence
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p A plethora of types of spectral sequences are special cases of the spectral sequence of a double complex, for instance
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%B6licher+spectral+sequence"}> Frölicher spectral sequence
              \.
          %p
            For the moment see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
            for a list.
          %h2#references References
          %p Dedicated discussion of the case of spectral sequences of double complexes is for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              Ravi Vakil,
              %em Spectral Sequences: Friend or Foe?
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.stanford.edu/~vakil/0708-216/216ss.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p or in section 25, lecture 9 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rick+Jardine"}> Rick Jardine
              ,
              %em Lectures on Homotopy Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uwo.ca/~jardine/papers/HomTh/lecture009.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Details are usually discussed for the more general case of a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+complex"} spectral sequence of a filtered complex
